{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":21797,"num_turns":2,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"f3b4863a-0b96-509e-86a9-b9a498414e2c","total_cost_usd":0.276719,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9168,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1769,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9168,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1769,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9168,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9168},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":4774,"outputTokens":23,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.004888999999999999,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty"},"claude-fable-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":1769,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":9168,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.27183,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-fable-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"declaration_consistent\":true,\"selected_report_demonstration\":\"issue\",\"lock_follows_declaration\":false,\"reasons\":[\"The declared independent-unit column plot_id is consistent with the frozen data: exactly 12 plot identifiers (PLOT-01 through PLOT-12) each appear in exactly 5 campaign rows, and each plot's treatment label is fixed across all its rows, yielding 6 biochar plots and 6 control plots, matching the data description for both procedure arms.\",\"The selected report demonstrates the issue on its face: it states that 12 plots were visited in 5 campaigns, then that 'each chamber measurement was entered as one replicate observation of its treatment, giving 30 observations per treatment', and the selected result reports a Welch two-sample t-test on 60 chamber measurements with df = 55.8. This shows the five repeated measurements from each plot (the declared independent unit) were entered into a row-independent two-sample t-test as if they were 60 independent replicates, when there are only 12 independent units (6 per arm).\",\"The workflow confirms the same: read_efflux pools every CSV row's co2_flux_umol_m2_s by treatment with no aggregation over plot_id before calling scipy.stats.ttest_ind, so within-plot dependence is ignored by the procedure.\",\"The lock's unit-key authorization does not follow from the declaration alone: the declaration establishes that plot_id is the independent unit and that each plot_id recurs five times in the input, so row-level entries keyed by plot_id are not independent. Authorizing scipy.stats.ttest_ind — a procedure that treats each row as an independent observation — as dependence-free over this input with authorized_key_columns ['plot_id'] contradicts, rather than follows from, that declaration; the authorization would only follow if plot_id were unique per row or the data were first aggregated to one value per plot.\"]}","structured_output":{"declaration_consistent":true,"selected_report_demonstration":"issue","lock_follows_declaration":false,"reasons":["The declared independent-unit column plot_id is consistent with the frozen data: exactly 12 plot identifiers (PLOT-01 through PLOT-12) each appear in exactly 5 campaign rows, and each plot's treatment label is fixed across all its rows, yielding 6 biochar plots and 6 control plots, matching the data description for both procedure arms.","The selected report demonstrates the issue on its face: it states that 12 plots were visited in 5 campaigns, then that 'each chamber measurement was entered as one replicate observation of its treatment, giving 30 observations per treatment', and the selected result reports a Welch two-sample t-test on 60 chamber measurements with df = 55.8. This shows the five repeated measurements from each plot (the declared independent unit) were entered into a row-independent two-sample t-test as if they were 60 independent replicates, when there are only 12 independent units (6 per arm).","The workflow confirms the same: read_efflux pools every CSV row's co2_flux_umol_m2_s by treatment with no aggregation over plot_id before calling scipy.stats.ttest_ind, so within-plot dependence is ignored by the procedure.","The lock's unit-key authorization does not follow from the declaration alone: the declaration establishes that plot_id is the independent unit and that each plot_id recurs five times in the input, so row-level entries keyed by plot_id are not independent. Authorizing scipy.stats.ttest_ind — a procedure that treats each row as an independent observation — as dependence-free over this input with authorized_key_columns ['plot_id'] contradicts, rather than follows from, that declaration; the authorization would only follow if plot_id were unique per row or the data were first aggregated to one value per plot."]},"ttft_ms":13228,"ttft_stream_ms":3224,"time_to_request_ms":10,"type":"result","duration_ms":20712,"uuid":"b5a525c4-f503-4b77-b06a-e0503cb67298"}
